          <md-tooltip>\n                      Provides deeper insights on your customers using Google data such as enhanced Audience and Demographics reporting.\n                    </md-tooltip>\n                    help_outline\n                  </i>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n              <div layout="column" layout-align="center center" class="google-signals-icons">\n                <i class="material-icons large-icon">google_my_business</i>\n                <div>\n                  All existing advertising features\n                  <i class="material-icons help-icon">\n                    <md-tooltip>\n                      Includes all existing advertising features such as demographics &amp; interests reports and remarketing.\n                    </md-tooltip>\n                    help_outline\n                  </i>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class="google-signals-explanation-section">\n              When you choose to activate Google signals, Google Analytics will associate the visitation information it collects from your site and/or apps with Google information from accounts of signed-in users who have consented to this association for the purpose of ads personalization. This Google information may include end user location, search history, YouTube history, and data from sites that partner with Google\u2014and is used to provide aggregated and anonymized insights into your users\' cross device behaviors. By enabling these features, you acknowledge you adhere to the <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/2700409" target="_blank"> Google Advertising Features Policy </a> , including rules around sensitive categories, have the necessary privacy disclosures and rights from your end users for such association, and that such data may be accessed and/or deleted by end users via <a href="https://myactivity.google.com/myactivity" target="_blank">My Activity</a>.\n            </div>\n            <div class="review-data-sharing-setting-section"\n                 ng-if="!$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled">\n              <div class="title">Review your data sharing settings</div>\n              <div ng-if="!$ctrl.settings.dataSharing.value.shareDataWithGoogle">\n                You <b>have not</b> enabled data sharing to help improve Google\'s products and services.\n              </div>\n              <div ng-if="$ctrl.settings.dataSharing.value.shareDataWithGoogle">\n                You <b>have</b> enabled data sharing to help improve Google\'s products and services.\n              </div>\n              The data sharing setting will also apply to authenticated visitation data collected by Google signals which is associated with Google user accounts. You acknowledge that you have the necessary rights from your end users, including disclosures in your privacy policy to share this data with Google. Enhanced Demographics and Interests Reporting is available only if you have enabled data sharing with Google.\n            </div>\n            <div ng-if="!$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled && !$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.value.getIsConsented()"\n                 layout="row"\n                 layout-align="end center">\n              <md-button ng-click="$ctrl.toggleConsentPanelState()"\n                         ng-disabled="$ctrl.uiDisabled"\n                         class="decide-later-button">\n                Decide later\n              </md-button>\n              <md-button ng-click="$ctrl.activateGoogleSignals()"\n                         ng-disabled="$ctrl.uiDisabled"\n                         class="activate-button md-primary md-raised">\n                Activate\n              </md-button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div ng-if="!$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled && !$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.value.getIsConsented() && !$ctrl.consentPanelExpanded"\n               layout="row"\n               layout-align="end">\n            <md-button class="md-primary md-raised get-started-button"\n                       ng-click="$ctrl.toggleConsentPanelState()">\n              Get started\n            </md-button>\n          </div>\n          <div class="enablement-status"\n               ng-if="$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.value.getIsConsented()">\n            <div ng-if="$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.value.getIsEnabled()"\n                 layout="row"\n                 layout-align="space-between center">\n              <div class="enabled-message">\n                Google signals is currently enabled for this project\n              </div>\n              <md-button ng-click="$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.callback(false)"\n                         ng-disabled="$ctrl.uiDisabled || $ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled"\n                         class=" md-primary disable-button">\n                Disable\n              </md-button>\n            </div>\n            <div ng-if="!$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.value.getIsEnabled()"\n                 layout="row"\n                 layout-align="space-between center">\n              <div class="disabled-message">\n                Google signals is currently disabled for this project\n              </div>\n              <md-button ng-click="$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.callback(true)"\n                         ng-disabled="$ctrl.uiDisabled || $ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled"\n                         class="md-primary  md-raised enable-button">\n                Enable\n              </md-button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class="disabled-settings-message-container"\n               ng-if="$ctrl.settings.googleSignals.disabled"\n               layout="row"\n               layout-align="start center">\n            <i class="material-icons grey-info-icon">\n              info\n            </i>\n            <div>\n              To make changes, visit your Google Analytics settings page.\n            </div>